<main class="lux-article-page"><nav class="lux-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en', '')); ?>">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/brand', '')); ?>">Brand News</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">LuxurEat (露意膳) at FHC Shanghai Global Food Trade Show</span></nav><article class="lux-reader-layout lux-event-seo-page"><div class="lux-reader-rule"></div><section class="lux-reader-hero"><div class="lux-reader-hero-copy"><div class="lux-reader-meta-grid"><span>Trade Fair</span><span>November 10–12, 2026</span><span>Shanghai</span></div><h1 id="lux-reader-title">LuxurEat (露意膳) at FHC Shanghai Global Food Trade Show</h1><p class="lux-reader-summary">From November 10 to 12, 2026, the 29th FHC Shanghai Global Food Trade Show will take place at the Shanghai New International Expo Centre. LuxurEat (露意膳) will present TruffleEat, CaviarEat, Ugolini, and other brands at Booth N3A10 in Hall N3.</p></div><figure class="lux-reader-cover"><img width="1920" height="620" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/events/fhc-shanghai-2026-banner.webp'); ?>" alt="LuxurEat (露意膳) at the 29th FHC Shanghai Global Food Trade Show"></figure></section><section class="lux-reader-content"><aside class="lux-reader-aside"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/brand', '')); ?>">Back to Brand News</a><span>Booth N3A10, Hall N3, Shanghai New International Expo Centre</span></aside><div class="lux-reader-copy"><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Event highlights</h2><p>With 28 years of experience in the food and beverage industry, FHC Shanghai is one of China’s most influential international trade shows. From Shanghai, it reaches across the Yangtze River Delta and connects with global markets, bringing together quality food and beverage producers, foodservice supply-chain businesses, and professional sourcing resources from around the world. The show provides an efficient platform for international brands entering China and Chinese companies expanding overseas.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Event scale</h2><p>In 2025, the show covered 200,000 square metres and welcomed more than 3,000 domestic and international exhibitors and 173,143 professional visitors. Attendees represented importers, distributors, agents, supermarkets and convenience stores, e-commerce and new retail, hotels and restaurants, coffee and tea, bakery and desserts, franchise chains, and other channels. Pavilions from more than 50 countries and regions showcased innovation and emerging trends across the global food and beverage industry.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Key areas</h2><p>The 29th FHC Shanghai Global Food Trade Show will again feature 15 exhibition sectors, including meat and seafood, snacks and beverages, dairy, confectionery and chocolate, condiments and cooking oils, coffee and tea, bakery and light meals, foodservice supply chains, and food processing and packaging. Business matching, product-selection events, industry forums, professional competitions, and media coverage will help exhibitors reach professional buyers, build visibility, and improve partnership efficiency.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Meet LuxurEat (露意膳)</h2><p>LuxurEat (露意膳) will present TruffleEat, CaviarEat, Ugolini, and other brands at Booth N3A10 in Hall N3, with a focused showcase of truffles, caviar, premium gourmet products, and solutions. Through FHC’s international platform, we look forward to meeting distributors, buyers, foodservice businesses, and industry partners to explore new opportunities in China and global food trade.</p></section><blockquote class="lux-reader-quote">Connecting with industry partners to explore new opportunities in China and global trade.</blockquote></div></section></article></main>
